{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch"],"anchor":"Articles"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionsandservices"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Atomic operations, savepoint nesting, transaction gating, and lifecycle hooks for cache invalidation."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/getService(_:)","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()"],"anchor":"Topics"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A transaction wraps a block of operations so they either all succeed and commit, or none of them are visible (rollback). LoomCore exposes this with a single method — the block is async, receives the database it runs on, and may suspend freely:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let fromID = 1","let toID = 2","let fromBalance = 90.0","let toBalance = 210.0","let journalID = 7","","try await db.transaction { db in","  try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO accounts (id, balance) VALUES (\\(fromID), \\(fromBalance))\")","  try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO accounts (id, balance) VALUES (\\(toID), \\(toBalance))\")","  try await db.exec(\"UPDATE journal SET state = \\(\"posted\") WHERE id = \\(journalID)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the block returns normally, the transaction commits. If it throws, the transaction rolls back and the error propagates. Atomicity is preserved across "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":"s inside the block — see the gating section below for how."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Lock modes","anchor":"Lock-modes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" selects the SQLite locking strategy:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/deferred","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — default; locks are acquired lazily as needed. Best concurrency, but writes can fail with ","type":"text"},{"code":"SQLITE_BUSY","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if another connection grabs the write lock first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/immediate","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — acquires the write lock at ","type":"text"},{"code":"BEGIN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Use when you know the transaction will write and want to fail fast.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/exclusive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — acquires an exclusive lock at ","type":"text"},{"code":"BEGIN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". No other connection can read or write. Use sparingly — typically only for migrations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["try await db.transaction(kind: .immediate) { db in","  \/\/ ...","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"type":"text","text":" applies to the outermost transaction only — nested calls open savepoints, which have no locking mode, so the parameter is ignored for them."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Nested transactions — savepoints","anchor":"Nested-transactions-savepoints"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calling "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside an active transaction opens a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SAVEPOINT"},{"type":"text","text":" scope. If the nested block returns normally, the savepoint is released and its work joins the enclosing transaction. If it throws, LoomCore rolls back to the savepoint — undoing only the nested block’s work, leaving the enclosing transaction intact — and rethrows the error:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct NoteRejected: Error {}","","let orderID = 1","let note = \"gift wrap, please\"","","try await db.transaction { db in","  try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO orders (id) VALUES (\\(orderID))\")","","  do {","    try await db.transaction { db in","      try await db.exec(\"INSERT INTO order_notes (order_id, note) VALUES (\\(orderID), \\(note))\")","      throw NoteRejected()","    }","  } catch is NoteRejected {","    \/\/ The note insert was rolled back; the order insert is still pending.","  }","","  \/\/ Commits the order (without the note).","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing inside a savepoint scope — released or not — becomes durable until the outermost transaction commits. Sibling child tasks that each open a nested transaction are serialized automatically by the gate, so their savepoint scopes never interleave (SQLite savepoints are a stack)."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Transaction gating","anchor":"Transaction-gating"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseActor"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its executor at every suspension point, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a transaction body would — without further machinery — let another task’s statements run inside the open transaction. LoomCore prevents this with a gate: while a transaction is in flight, even while its body is suspended, database operations from tasks "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"outside"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the transaction suspend and resume once the transaction commits or rolls back."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Membership is tracked by a task-local token bound around the block:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Structured children","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"async let","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", task groups) and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"unstructured ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task {}","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" inherit the token and operate inside the transaction. An unstructured task must complete before the body returns (await its value); a task that outlives the body races the commit and may run outside the transaction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Task.detached","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" does not inherit it — a detached task waits at the gate like any outside caller. Awaiting a detached task’s database work from inside the transaction body therefore deadlocks.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An operation waiting at the gate throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if its task is cancelled.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once past the gate, an operation runs to completion synchronously on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseActor"},{"type":"text","text":" — interleaving between tasks happens only at gates and suspension points, never mid-statement. When no transaction is active the gate is a single nil check, so ungated workloads pay essentially nothing."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Services — lifecycle hooks","anchor":"Services-lifecycle-hooks"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Subclass "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to react to transaction lifecycle events. Common uses are cache invalidation, change notifications, and audit logging:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@DatabaseActor","final class Cache {","  private var entries: [String: Int] = [:]","","  func invalidateAll() {","    entries.removeAll()","  }","}","","final class CacheInvalidator: Database.Service {","  let cache = Cache()","","  override func transactionDidCommit() {","    cache.invalidateAll()","  }","}","","let invalidator = await db.getService(CacheInvalidator.self)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Services are singletons per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Database"},{"type":"text","text":" instance and per service type. The first "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/getService(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" call constructs the service via the inherited "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(database:)"},{"type":"text","text":"; subsequent calls return the same instance. Use stored-property defaults (or override "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(database:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to set them up) for any per-service state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Services receive "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionWillBegin()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidCommit()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidRollback()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"only for the outermost physical transaction"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". Nested (savepoint) scopes fire no callbacks — they describe intermediate state that only becomes durable when the outer transaction commits. Implicit per-statement transactions (a bare "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exec"},{"type":"text","text":" outside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transaction"},{"type":"text","text":" block) do not fire service callbacks either."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What rollback failure means","anchor":"What-rollback-failure-means"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some failures roll the physical transaction back inside SQLite itself — an interrupted write ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or task cancellation) and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ON CONFLICT ROLLBACK"},{"type":"text","text":" constraints both do. LoomCore detects that, skips its own now-pointless "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ROLLBACK"},{"type":"text","text":", still notifies services via "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidRollback()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and rethrows the block’s error with the connection intact. From that point the body can no longer write: any further statement or nested transaction throws "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/LoomCoreErrorCode\/transactionScopeLost","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", so catching the failed write and carrying on cannot leave rows committed one by one outside the transaction."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ROLLBACK"},{"type":"text","text":" itself fails on a transaction that is genuinely still open (rare — typically only a corrupt or disconnected database), LoomCore logs a warning, closes the underlying handle, and rethrows the original error from the block. Subsequent operations on the database fail with a closed-database error."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Transaction-control SQL is the caller’s responsibility","anchor":"Transaction-control-SQL-is-the-callers-responsibility"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"LoomCore does not inspect statements for transaction control. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BEGIN"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"COMMIT"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"END"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ROLLBACK"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SAVEPOINT"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RELEASE"},{"type":"text","text":" passed to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exec"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"query"},{"type":"text","text":" run as-is, bypassing the transaction gate and the service hooks — using them is at your own risk:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inside "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)"}]},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"COMMIT","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes the work durable, yet the scope then finds the physical transaction gone: it throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/LoomCoreErrorCode\/transactionScopeLost","type":"reference"},{"text":" and notifies services via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service\/transactionDidRollback()","type":"reference"},{"text":" for data that was committed. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"ROLLBACK","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" discards the work the same way. Any further statement in the body throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/LoomCoreErrorCode\/transactionScopeLost","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Outside a transaction"}]},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BEGIN"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SAVEPOINT"},{"text":" opens a transaction the gate knows nothing about. Other tasks’ operations are not held back, so their writes silently join it and commit or roll back with it, and a later ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" fails at its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"BEGIN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" until it is closed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prefer "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/execScript(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for a script that balances its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BEGIN … COMMIT"},{"type":"text","text":". When you do manage a transaction by hand, make sure nothing else uses the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Database"},{"type":"text","text":" until it is closed."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Handling SQLITE_BUSY","anchor":"Handling-SQLITEBUSY"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A second connection — another process, or another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Database"},{"type":"text","text":" on the same file — can hold a lock that makes a statement fail with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SQLiteResultCode\/busy"},{"type":"text","text":". Three tools, in the order to reach for them:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — SQLite retries the lock inside ","type":"text"},{"code":"sqlite3_step","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for up to the timeout before failing. Keep it modest: the wait sleeps while holding the global ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/DatabaseActor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", stalling every ","type":"text"},{"code":"Database","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the process for its duration. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/interrupt()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (and task cancellation) aborts a busy wait.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/immediate"}]},{"text":" — a transaction that will write should fail fast at ","type":"text"},{"code":"BEGIN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rather than mid-transaction after doing work.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Retry at the call site"}]},{"text":" — for contention that outlasts a reasonable timeout:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func withBusyRetry<T>(_ attempts: Int = 3, _ body: () async throws -> T) async throws -> T {","  for _ in 0..<(attempts - 1) {","    do {","      return try await body()","    } catch let error as LoomError where error.sqlite == .busy {","      try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(50))","    }","  }","  return try await body()","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enabling WAL mode ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setJournalMode(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") also removes most reader\/writer contention between connections to the same file.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"LoomCore"}],"title":"Transactions and Services","role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setBusyTimeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"milliseconds"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5Int32V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int32"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5Int32V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int32"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Sets the busy timeout and returns the value actually applied.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/setbusytimeout(milliseconds:)","title":"setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setBusyTimeout(milliseconds:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/setJournalMode(_:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setJournalMode"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Database","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"JournalMode","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC11JournalModeO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"text":"Database","preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC11JournalModeO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"JournalMode"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets the journal mode and returns the mode actually applied."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/setjournalmode(_:)","title":"setJournalMode(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/setJournalMode(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/transaction(kind:_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transaction"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore15TransactionKindO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TransactionKind"},{"kind":"text","text":", ("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore8DatabaseC","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Database"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"text":"T","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Runs a block of operations atomically inside a transaction.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/transaction(kind:_:)","title":"transaction(kind:_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/transaction(kind:_:)"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/Service":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Service","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Base class for cross-cutting database services that hook into transaction lifecycle events."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Service","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/service","title":"Database.Service","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/TransactionKind":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TransactionKind"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TransactionKind"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SQLite transaction locking mode."}],"title":"TransactionKind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionkind"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/TransactionKind/exclusive":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"exclusive"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Acquires an exclusive lock when the transaction begins."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionkind\/exclusive","title":"TransactionKind.exclusive","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionKind\/exclusive","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/getService(_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"getService"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the singleton instance of "},{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for this database, creating it on first access."}],"title":"getService(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/getService(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/getservice(_:)"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/QueryingJSON":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract, filter, modify, build, and iterate JSON documents with typed expressions over SQLite’s JSON functions."}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/queryingjson","title":"Querying JSON","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/SQLiteResultCode/busy":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"busy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8LoomCore16SQLiteResultCodeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SQLiteResultCode"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Database file could not be written because of concurrent activity by another